.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt BASENAME 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm basename
.Nd print final components of path strings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar name Op Ar suffix
.Nm
.Op Fl az
.Op Fl s Ar suffix
.Ar name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Remove leading directory components and trailing separators from each
path string and print the final component.
This is a string operation: the named object need not exist and no file
is opened.
With two operands in the simple form, the second is a suffix to remove
only when it matches and would not remove the whole name.
.Pp
.Fl a
accepts multiple names rather than interpreting the second as a suffix.
.Fl s Ar suffix
selects suffix removal and also enables multiple names.
.Fl z
terminates results with NUL rather than newline.
Use
.Ql --
before a name beginning with a dash.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; nonzero for missing/extra operands, invalid options
or output failure. Diagnostics use standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
basename /home/operator/notes.txt .txt
.Ed
.Sh ABSD PROFILE
This is the unmodified uutils 0.12.0 utility pinned by the platform build.
The reference describes selected source-supported options; use
.Fl Fl help
for the complete upstream interface.
File access uses the process's ABSD filesystem view, output uses its
inherited stream, and the command acquires no additional authority.
There are no native Unix processes, signals or permission bits underneath
this port.
The command matrix exercises the example forms below; other options
listed here are source-checked, not separately guest-qualified.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr intro 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
